v3.2.4
Radon Player 3.2.4: One scan, one place
## 3.2.4: One scan, one place (Windows and Android)
- **No made-up moods:** a song gets moods only from Scan moods, its file's MOOD tag, your own picks or your other device; the guess from the genre alone is gone. After Remove all moods the Moods tab is really empty until you scan (the genre guesses made it look as if moods were still in the files).
- **Dual on Now playing:** Now playing's visualizer button has a Dual switch: pick one style for the middle (around the cover) and one for the bottom, and both play at once, no need to make your own. It's in Settings › Personalization too.
- **Wrapped and lyrics card styles in Personalization:** Settings › Personalization has Wrapped style and Lyrics card style menus (they stay in Wrapped and the Lyrics card box too), so everything about how the app looks is in one place, and a Personalization preset now keeps the Dual visualizer, Wrapped's style and the lyrics card's style as well.
- **Pine forest fixed:** the trees all stand on the bottom edge now (the back row used to float above it), each one solid tree of three tiers on a short trunk (no darker patches where the tiers overlap), sized to the space (no wall of trees in a small preview), and the effect takes its own colour when you pick one.
- **All your personalization in backups and Sync:** your own looks, layouts, visualizers and colour blends, Wrapped styles, lyrics card styles, Personalization presets and now your saved colours too are all in backups, and each Sync adds the other device's to yours (one deleted on either is gone from both). Each device still wears its own look, theme and layout; pick a preset to put the same setup on the other one.
- **One mood scan:** Scan moods, Full scan and Read moods from lyrics are one scan now. Scan moods hears each song whole and reads its words (by the AI when it's on), and only once both are done writes the song's moods (and its words' reading) into its file, so the sound always has its say before anything is written.
- **Moods go into the files only from the scan:** the Write moods into the files tick is gone; nothing writes moods into your files but Scan moods (and moods you pick yourself in the Tagger).
- **Scanned once:** the app keeps track of every song it has scanned and never scans it again; Settings › Reset mood and lyrics scans is the only way to start over. A song whose moods aren't in its file yet (the playing song, moods from your other device) just has them written by the next scan, with nothing heard again.
- **Settings resets for the one scan:** Reset moods works the moods out again from what was heard and read (nothing heard again) and the next Scan moods writes them in; Reset sound scan and Remove all moods are followed by Scan moods too.

### Good to know
- **Android:** install RadonPlayer.apk over 3.2.3 (same signature, your library and settings stay), or tap Update in Settings.
- **Windows:** Radon-Player-3.2.4.msi installs over 3.2.3, or use Update in Settings.
- **Moods:** after updating, tap Scan moods on the Moods tab once: it hears each song whole and reads its words, then writes its moods into its file. A song is scanned only once.
